caption:
cool spots in atl for you to save & share 

follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

Add these to ur list 
@kinjoroom is moody and sexy and the perfect spot for gno or date night. Fill the table with sushi and cocktails and have yourself an evening. You can find them in @theinterlockatl in west midtown. 
@krogbar_pizza_ has the perfect neighborhood vibe with a cozy interior and a coal fired pizza oven. They don’t take reservations fyi. Find them in peachtree hills by Lindbergh. 
@fumatl speaks for itself with a vinyl dj playing in front of a chef making fresh pasta, an open kitchen and a cured meat room on display. It’s contemporary Italian from a Michelin rated team in Mia. Find them in @starmetalsatl in west midtown. 

Which one are you going to first??

Have you been to this (hidden?) gem yet!? 

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌 this is part 3💫

@bona_fide_deluxe is one of my favorite casual spots to hang out in Atlanta. They have some of the best sandwiches in Atlanta like the smoked turkey, that one is a must. It’s a really cute spot next to a wine bar which makes for a good walkable date night if you haven’t been yet, add this to your list! I’m so sorry I’m late. How are you put that in?

Because I know you love a vibe 👇

Follow @atllovesmo for more ✨

@georgiaboyatlanta is one of the most unique and delicious meals I’ve had in Atlanta. Created by James Beard nominated @chefjoeyward, the menu is full of surprising twists on dishes inspired by his Georgia roots. I can guarantee there is a dish on the 14-16 course pre-fixe menu that will make you ~smile.  You should check out this cleverly hidden speakeasy restaurant meant to spark joy & nostalgia. 

@stceciliaatl is one of the most stunning restaurants in Buckhead perfect for date night (so stunning it has been featured in tv shows). They’ve have a menu full of freshly made pasta & seafood and one of the best bread services in atlanta. End the night with soft serve gelato and an espresso martini. You can’t go wrong! 

@ryokou.atl is one of those meals I’ve been dreaming of since sitting at the 10 person chefs counter. You get a full view of the masters at work as they prepare each course. It’s fun and interactive and unlike your traditional omakase experience. The entire menu is intentional and expertly planned out, with fish and other ingredients flown in from Japan. It’s one of those treat yourself meals you absolutely deserve. 

Save for your next date night, birthday meal, or night out with friends 🫶

#Atlblog #atlantafood #thingstodoinatl

psa: @buckheadrestaurantweek by @livablebuckhead is here 7/21-7/26

Enjoy specially priced lunch & dinner specials all week long in Buckhead! 

 @brushatl is one of my favorite spots for sushi and nigiri in Atlanta. They have a unique menu set in a beautiful upscale space. You can participate in Buckhead restaurant week during lunch ($30 pre-fixe) or dinner ($75 pre-fixe) which includes choices for each course including dessert (their pastry selection is next level). 

@lebilboquetatlanta is the perfect summertime spot. It’s a French restaurant with a charming patio sure to transport you to Europe. It’s one of my favorite spots to grab a spritz with the girls. More information to drop soon on their restaurant week menu! 

@carmelatl is a truly breathtaking seafood restaurant with coastal flavors that transport you to your favorite seaside destinations ✨ they have a stunning bar where you can sip coastal cocktails before dinner. $65 per person | $45 drink pairing for their restaurant week menu which includes choice of app, entree, dessert. 

The vibes at each of these spots are immaculate making for a cute date night, girls night, or solo trip to the bar. Find them all in @buckheadvillagedistrict. 

Head to buckheadrestaurantweek.com to see the menus! 

If you love date night inspo, follow @atllovesmo 💌

#atlfoodie #atleats #atlantafood #atlblog

These are all perfect date spots in the city so be sure to save & share 🫶

follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

@redactedbasementdrinkparlor is a cool underground  cocktail lounge with good vibes and unique cocktails!! They have options like the fruit loop milk punch or the Saturn with Valley Gin, orgeat, velvet falernum, lemon, & passionfruit. Grab dinner before or after a visit here in @summerhill_atl. 

@sammysatl is now open in Adair park and I fear you should run there for their matcha, their lattes, and their sandwiches (like the Cuban made with locally sourced bread from a Cuban bakery on Buford hwy). All of their sandwiches are insane and made w looove (& meats smoked in house). Right now they’re open Monday-Friday 7-3pm as they get started but lots of exciting things to come from them! 

@avize.atl sister cocktail bar, @bar.avize , is everything I dream of - good cocktails, stunning interior, and an elevated bar menu to match (completely different from the dining experience at Avize). The patio will be the spot to be during spring, especially considering they have bougie chicken nuggies with hot honey, (salmon) caviar, & creme fraiche. There’s also a late night burger on the menu 9pm & on with freshly baked bread (only 20 sold so jump on it). 

What’s your pick?? 

#atlblog #atleats #atlfoodie

The most magical beltline parade is back on the Southwest Trail on Saturday, May 3 ✨💫

Send to a friend & follow @atllovesmo for more 🪩

Lantern Parade Schedule

4:00 p.m.: Vendor market and food trucks open at 1200 White Street.
5:00-7:00 p.m.: Lantern-making stations and vendor market are open at the Atlanta Beltline Marketplace @ Allene (1089 Allene Avenue, S.W.).
7:35 p.m.: Line-up begins for the parade in Adair Park I (742 Catherine St SW).
8:35 p.m.: The parade begins and steps off onto the Southwest Trail.
9:15 p.m.-10:00 p.m.: All of the bands and the puppets join for a jam session and parade finale in the Lee + White Food Hall parking lot.
11:00 p.m.: 1200 White Street activations close for the night.

Participating Bands

@atlantadrumacademy 
@atlantafreedombands 
@blacksheepensemble 
@mausikiscalescommonground 
@seedandfeed marching abominable 
@kebbiwilliams and the Wolfpack’

psa you can make your own lanterns!! Parade creator @chantellerytter and the Krewe of the Grateful Gluttons are hosting a series of free and paid workshops at their studio! 

I always like to catch the end when everyone congregates in the parking lot and the bands perform! You can also post up along the beltline with a chair. 

#atlblog #atlfoodie #thingstodoinatlanta #atldatenight

You dont have to leave atl to feel like youre in Peru 

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

@madreselvaatl will transport you to Peru with their different types of ceviche and stunning interior. There’s a new outdoor patio perfect for sipping pisco sours in the breezy spring weather. You’ll feel like you’ve been hanging out on the coast. The traditional Latin flavors have been elevated and not only taste soooo freaking good but have been beautifully plated as well. The team really crushed it with this one. It’s one of the most beautiful bars in atlanta. Can’t promise the llamas will be there next time but they’ll always be there in spirit. 🥲🫶

@madreselvaatl makes for a cute date night or go solo at the fish counter ✨ save & share ✨

#atlblog #atleats #atlfoodie

if you’re looking for places to take your friends from out of town 👇 

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

@blockanddrum is a gem in @chamblee.ga. It’s a listening bar and distillery with a hydroponic farm, which means good vibes and good cocktails. The space has been completely converted into what feels like an adult playground in the best way. There is a giant screen in a large green space and a dj booth for vinyl spinning and more. There’s also a cafe, so yeah, add it to ur list! Thanks @atlantacoffeeshops for the rec! 

@madreselvaatl will transport you to Peru with their different types of ceviche and stunning interior. There’s a new outdoor patio perfect for sipping pisco sours in the breezy spring weather. You’ll feel like you’ve been hanging out on the coast. The traditional Latin flavors have been elevated and not only taste soooo freaking good but have been beautifully plated as well. 

@wagyuhouseatl easily has some of the best views in the city. This is definitely one of the best spots to hang out in west midtown. What’s better than a little rooftop Japanese BBQ & all you can eat items ✨ they have some rules for dining so be sure to check it out beforehand. 

All of the above would make for great spots to hang with your friends or have a cute date night. If you have some recs, I’m all ears. 

#atlblog #atleats #atlfoodie

new on the beltine!! add to your list 🫶

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

@yujiatlanta has soft opened on the corner of the beltline over in @thekrogdistrictatl and it’s perfection. The interior is stunning with a chefs counter and gorgeous bar. The patio is not quite open yet, but once spring hits this will be the spot to hang out. You can go for sushi, nigiri, wagyu, seafood bisque (a must), branzino, & more just leave room for desert. 

Perfect for date night, gno, or a solo date at the bar/ chefs counter. You’re going to love it. 

@alexkinjo crushes it every time ✨

#atleats #atlfoodie #atlbeltline @atlantabeltline

three new spots for you to try in atl ✨👇

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

I love a vibe, you love a vibe, so here are some places you need to check out that fit the bill. 

@yujiatlanta has been highly anticipated right on the @atlantabeltline and it’s stunning. You can watch the magic happen at the chefs counter, solo dine at the beautiful bar or gather your friends for one perfectly yummy meal. Planning an immediate trip back. The cocktails, the fresh seafood, the creative dishes, the ambiance - all were 10/10. Plus, it’s perfect for a walkable date. 

@madeiraparkatl has just opened their doors to us in Poncey-Highland and it’s a proper wine bar with an extensive list to ogle over. It’s more on the casual side and gives the neighborhood feel that’s vibrant but relaxed. It comes from some pretty talented minds so we’re in for a treat. Be sure to make a reservation before you go. 

@boqueria is another new find in @colonysquareatl which is a cult classic in other states. It’s a Spanish tapas bar and restaurant set inside a really stunning space. The carrots were to die for and what’s better than wine & charcuterie. Overall I thought the menu was fairly affordable for the vibe so it’ll make a good date night. Since tapas are meant to be shared you should absolutely try a lil of everything. 

Which one are you going to first ?? 

#atlblog #atleats #atlfoodie #atldatenight

