Where should we go in 2025?? ⬇️

@nadairatl is on my list!

#atleats #atlblog #atlantafood #martinimo

On a mission to find all of the underground Christmas pop ups in atlanta that are worth going to and @gabeergarden is one of them. They’ve launched the Worst Christmas Bar where your traditional beer garden meets Old Saint Nick with tacky decor, creative cocktails and a ridiculously good food menu. Instead of traditional bar food they have deviled eggs, brussel sprouts, crispy sweet potatoes, macha stuffed quail and short rib with a cornbread pancake by @malskitchenatl. Reserve on @toasttab 

@independent_distilling is easily one of my favorite places for a cocktail based on their menu, their incredible service, and the laid back atmosphere. It’s located in an old auto shop that’s currently decked out in holiday spirit and the cocktails are unique (one features duck egg). They put a spin on the classics like one of my favorites the Decatur Daiquiri with fresh pressed cane juice. If you were curious about the egg get Santa’s Little Helper with Independent Aged Rum, Buttermilk, Duck Egg, Maple Syrup, Bitters, Nutmeg and Smoked Paprika (so creamy and delicious)! 

I’m a big fan of getting dressed up & going to Christmas bars and this is one you should add to your list. @westside_motor_lounge has two different bars on site giving all of the cozy vibes with ridiculously great decorations (& maybe even a Santa sighting). You could also hang outside by the fire pits and play a game of shuffleboard or corn hole. This is a great spot for a big group of people. Grab your friends and get in the holiday spirit, it’s time!! make sure you stop by Echo Room for vinyl spinning and more festive cocktails. 

@homefortheholidaysatl is straight out of a 1950s post card and one to make you feel warm & cozy. It’s an $82 4-course prefixe menu with bread service (that includes gratuity already). The menu features lamb eggrolls and smoked beet tartare which you must try. The bread service is insane with the fermented butter (bury me in that). You can add on oysters and cavair too if youre feeling fancy. The steak frites are a MUST in my option to pair with your winter cocktails. Make a reservation on @resy or walk-in by mentioning atllovesmo.

three spots to add to your list 👇

Follow @atllovesmo for more 💌

@tigersunatl is a vintage bus that has been completely reimagined with orange shaggy carpet, big fuzzy chairs, a bar in the back and funky neon lights. They’re changing the way we do cocktails with an immersive curated cocktail omakase type menu where the four drinks have all been paired with creative culinary enhancements designed to complement each one. Reservations will be released at 10 AM every other Tuesday in two week reservation blocks on @resy. Set your calendar! There are 18 seats total and I promise you want to make sure you’re in one of them for the first menu inspired by Karate Kid.

The new cozy & dimly lit steakhouse @ilpremioatlanta at @forthatlanta is a goodie! The menu here features some incredible seafood options to start (the yellowtail is a must), handmade pasta (like the short rib agnolotti or bolognese), and premium steaks and sides. Couldn’t pass up the truffle mac & cheese and the broccolini that had a lil kick to it. This has been one of my favorite meals this year, especially thanks to that perfectttt dry aged Kansas City strip. 

@twourbanlicks celebrated 20 years in business recently and that’s obviously saying something! It’s located steps from the beltline (as are all of these actually). There is almost always live music and good energy. Pair that with a delicious meal and you’re all set. I’m sure you’ve heard of the iconic salmon chips which is a great place to start. This makes for another cute date night spot. 

#atleats #atlfoodie #thingstodoinatlanta #atlblog

Save & share some of the best ~haunted spots~ to celebrate spooky season in Atlanta 👇

Follow @atllovesmo x @atlannatonight x @knotts01 for more inspo 👻

Here’s a quick rundown of some spooky spots around Atlanta, complete with important details for each:

@netherworldhauntedhouse is atl’s most iconic haunted attraction. It’s open from September 22 through November 11. Tickets start at $25, with options for a speed pass. Get ready for two new haunts this year: “Wake the Dead” and “Mr. Grendel’s Birthday Party of Horrors”​ 📍located at 1313 Netherworld Way, Stone Mountain, GA

Six Flags Fright Fest: Head over to @sixflagsovergeorgia in Austell for their annual Fright Fest, happening on select nights through October 31. Regular admission is required, with additional fees for haunted attractions. During the day, it’s family-friendly with trick-or-treat trails, but after 6 PM, it becomes a scare zone with haunted mazes and live actors around every corner.

@hauntedundergroundatl at @underground_atlanta is one of my favs. The over the top Halloween decor is 10/10, giving all of the dark, moody, spooky vibes you’re looking for. Bring allll of your friends or have a fun & funky date night. You can get your ticket for an early session 8-11pm or late night 11-4am. 

Be sure to use code ATLLOVESMO (we love a deal). 🔗 in bio 

@rrealtacos has locations all over the city that are decked out for the season. They’re pulling out all of the stops with a Halloween-themed taco and creative cocktails! Open all month long! They don’t require tickets, but it’s best to make a reservation if you’re planning a weekend visit.

@drawbaratl at @bellyardhotel has gone spooky with their rooftop patio! Located in West Midtown, Drawbar is hosting a Halloween party on October 28 with themed cocktails, DJ sets, and costume contests. Perfect for a spooky night out to celebrate the season! 

Which are you going to first? 

#atlblog #thingstodoinatlanta #atldatenight

Three 3 spots to share with your friends ✨ we looove a vibe 

Follow @atllovesmo for more 🪩

@commune_atl is a listening bar in Avondale estates and it’s a goodie. Expect a variety of music from live jazz and good tunes from DJ’s spinning vinyl. It’s a speakeasy located in @_oliveandpine_ (if you think you’re not supposed to walk through there you’re in the right place). Go for the wine and the music. The wine list is expansive and they have some small bites as well. If you love a vibe, this is for you.

@pendolinoatl is a beautiful restaurant in SS pulling inspiration for their menu from different regions of Italy. Rather than transporting you to a different country, they’re keeping you in the neighborhood with a cozy & welcoming atmosphere and a modern, southernized Italian menu. Pair your wood-fired pizza with a grapefruit spritz and your chicken parmesan with a beautifully crafted wine. It’s the perfect date night spot 🍝

@barblancatlanta is one of my favorites on the west side and let me tell youuu it is beautiful. They’re serving the most lux $50 prefixe menu including a fresh loaf of bread, salad, pomme frites and steak. I could swim in the bearnaise sauce 🤤 don’t skip the dessert either!! no reservations required for a visit. Its small interior leads to the most cozy, elevated atmosphere and the perfect spot for a date night, a solo dine, or celebratory dinner. It’s almost patio weather and their patio seating is giving all of the European vibes we’re looking for. 

Which one are you going to first??

Your next night out should look like this!

@sfseav is a quirky food hall in East Atlanta Village that is perfect for hanging out with friends (even late night - 4am 👀). They have a variety of food from Brazilian pizza to speciality waffles and more. Look out for events like open mic night & live music + dance nights (✍️reggae dub afro-funk is coming up on 9/20). Check it out: 

@butecoatl is a Brazilian coffee and cocktail bar that features perfect syrups made in house and interesting cocktails. You know a caipirinha must be on the menu - choose between passion fruit, coconut, lime & guava. You’ll find your fav PSL and a banana mocha on the coffee specials so 🏃 there now. 

@buenapapafrybar is where you go when you need your potato fix. Build your own handcut loaded fries & baked potatoes layered with melted cheese and all the best toppings or go with their different creations spanning the world (think Mexicano with carne asada, guac + more). Don’t skip the freshly prepared churros OR the jugo naturales (mango juice). 

@brasilianaus is a Brazilian pizza spot where you can order whole pies or by the slice! You must try a Brazilian classic like the chicken catupiry which features cheese widely used in Brazil. You’ll find Brazilian & American ingredients with unique flavors and long fermentation crust in their savory & sweet pizzas. The Nutella pizza is a MUST!!

@sinfulslidrz gives you everything you want in craft original sliders. Be sure to get the Caribbean style oxtail with plantains and the 16-hr cola brisket sliders!! They also have a low country shrimp patty, fresh salmon patty, + more. You can even build your own from scratch if you’re feeling fun.

Do you ever just crave perfect fluffy waffles bc same. @_waffle_bar has a creative menu of Belgian waffles (even gluten free + vegan). The blueberry crunch cake was incredible & guarantee I’m trying the banana pudding next time. They’ll also surprise you with ridiculously good jerk pasta with fried salmon that I’m still thinking about. 

Everyone knows & loves Woodys Cheesesteaks in atl for their classic steak & chicken sandwiches or a cold cut with a milkshake. The perfect late night meal does exist!!

with European flare & a beautiful patio to sip on a Hugo spritz ✨

@lebilboquetatlanta is an incredibly beautiful spot in @buckheadvillagedistrict perfect for your next girls night out! It’s also perfect for a walkable date (those who get it, get it). The patio is the best part. Whether you stop in while shopping or go for nice night out, add this to your list. You’ll want to wear something cute & dressy. Rumor has it they have a great espresso martini. I promise to report back. Right now, I’m a hugo spritz girlie (clearly we all are) especially in this heat! 

Share with your spritz loving friends 🫶

You’re going to want to check out these cute spots, trust me ✨

You need to know about this hidden gem in atl with Mediterranean fare, a quaint patio, and the best priced wine in the city. I finally made my way to @kittydareatl in @inmanpark, which is a glimpse into various Mediterranean cultures and an incredible wine menu curated by owner Jaamy (well known for his time spent at Last Resort Grill) and executive chef Giuseppe (who brings in his influence from his Italian heritage). Every detail of the restaurant is thoughtfully planned, including the beautiful back patio that transports you out of Atlanta and into the Mediterranean. It’s the perfect spot to enjoy a bottle of Berlucchi ‘61. My favorite dishes of the night were the labneh, gnocchi, and the bucatini and shrimp. Whatever you do, make sure you get the white chocolate pistachio cheesecake (and maybe an espresso martini to pair). 

@lamoon_atl is a favorite of mine in @virginiahighlanddistrict with its shotgun interior, beautiful back patio, and most deliciousss menu. The vibe is perfect inside, especially on a nice day with the big window open. Their menu spans from shaking beef to dumplings to clay pot dishes and lobster tail tempura fried rice. You already know I can’t turn down a lychee spritz but they also have the basil bliss with drops of basil oil that is to die for. This should be an immediate save. Let me know what you think when you go! 

@ela.atlanta is another favorite of mine in @virginiahighlanddistrict. They feature a delicious Mediterranean menu with brunch, happy hour, and dinner. The cocktails were perfection like the Great Asp! and the Spice Road (with mezcal and blood orange) 🍊 the menu makes for a good time sharing food like the mezze board which is almost a right of passage with labneh, hummus, and eggplant dip. I can also speak to the incredible flavors of the hot chicken and spinach feta hot pocket (like my childhood but 30x better). Skewers and couscous pairing for dinner plus baklava froyo then call it a night!! I can also confirm the brunch menu shouldn’t be missed. Yet another goodie to add to your list. 

#atlfoodie #atleats #atlthaifood #atlblog #atldatenight

✨It’s time!! for fun things to do in atl ➡️ follow @atllovesmo 

@gvgatl’s A Day at the Dairies is back tomorrow 6/9 from 12-6pm (and it’s free!). Have yourself the best day with breakfast at @homegrownga, vintage shopping at @atlantadairies, followed by a beer or three at @3timaginarium. 

@gvgatl hosts an array of events each month supporting local artists, vintage curators and handmade artisans (they’re pro’s they’ve been supporting the community since 2014). I stopped in at their bi-monthly event “A Day at Dairies” in Reynoldstown @atlantadairies. This is a must visit market in Atlanta. Find everything from plants, vinyl, vintage clothing, art, and so much more. 

GVG has been hosting vintage and handmade pop ups around Atlanta for close to 10 years to encourage you to #supporttinybusinesses ✨ you’re bound to find something fun & funky that you can’t find anywhere else!!

Keep your eyes peeled for @topochicousa and @therounds.co 

#atlmarket #atlvintage #atlantablog #thingstodoinatlanta #atleats

@shakykneesfest is the place the be ✨good music + @redbull watermelon margs makes for a good weekend. If you haven’t been to Shaky, take this as a sign to go. Even with the monsoon people were dancing in puddles with their friends & slip and sliding to Billy Joel (I hid in the bathroom with 20 other ladies so it was a great bonding moment lol, if you’re one of them and you’re reading this - hiii👋🏼). 10/10 put @shakykneesfest on your calendar next year! 

Follow @atllovesmo for fun things to do in Atlanta 💌

#atlfestival #atlblog #atlfoodie #shakyknees #shakykneesfest #redbull

pov: looking for lunch spots in Atlanta 🥪✨🌮🍴 this is a request I get often so here is part 1 👉 be sure to save for later

💌 follow @atllovesmo for more good food in atl 

@birdcageatl is bringing you all the Latin flavors to Grant Park with citrus adobo chicken straight off the grill so you can build your own tacos. It’s an affordable spot for lunch with a half chicken plate being $12. I’m still thinking about the red chicken tacos with a special shoutout to those sweet potato bravas. On a nice day, they’ll have the giant windows open for some indoor/ outdoor dining.

@dipsdipsdipskitchen in @poncecitymarket is revolutionizing the way we dip with grab & go dips that are ready to enjoy on the spot or at home. This would make for a great picnic lunch with the nice weather approaching. They have classics like spinach artichoke dip and buffalo chicken dip as well as vegan and gluten free options. Choose your “chip” and get to dipping. 

@fraziesmeatandmarket in @riversideatl is a neighborhood favorite with unique chef driven sandwiches and local goods. They’ve been open less than a year & you’ll be asking yourself why you haven’t been in sooner after that first bite. The southern gentleman is a spin on a childhood classic, with @fripperssausages fried bologna and green onion pimento cheese on fresh ciabatta bread. This sandwich started it all and is one you must try!

#atlfoodie #atleats #atlantafood #atlblog

Beautiful, low key spots in Atlanta for a good dinner? I got you 

💌 follow along if you aren’t already @atllovesmo 

Your next date night, girls night out, or solo dinner should be at one of these spots. Which one would you go to first? 

@brushatl is the incredibly beautiful Japanese restaurant in  @buckheadvillagedistrict with some of the best sushi in Atlanta. They also have an intimate omakase service as well as an upcoming tuna cutting. It’s elegant and elevated and would make a great birthday dinner. Put on your cutest outfit and have a ridiculously good dinner ✨

@elvinedolocal will transport you to South America. It is a wine bar, a coffee shop, and a tapas bar nestled in Midtown. There is a large communal table running down the middle and is a great spot to gather with friends. Pair your wine with arepas, empanadas, and ceviche. Whether you go for coffee in the morning or an evening date night, you’ll love it 💫 pro tip: don’t forget to check out @atlantarestaurantclub 🔗 in bio 

@gaja_eav is a hidden gem in EAV with the coolest atmosphere and delicious Korean bites. Find the entrance at the back of a brick building, when you find the neon sign that reads Korean food, you’ll know you’re in the right place. The focus is small plates so order one of everything to share with the table. The cocktails were easily also one of my favorite parts, like the country honey with mezcal and chili oil and honey 🍯 

#atlfoodie #atlantaeats #atldatenight #atleats

more deets on these fun, reoccurring events around the city👇 

💌 follow @atllovesmo if you love to explore Atlanta 

@_artandb_ is a mixture of music, art, and community. Think art show meets r&b party. You get to support local artists, mingle, drink, dance, even get a tattoo from an artist on site. There’s an open bar for the first hour and hookah and food (free tacos at the next event). Mark your calendar for 5/5 at Westside Cultural Center @westsideartsctr 🖼️

@mysticdistrictmarket is another unique event to support local small businesses and & tickets can be found in my bio! Use code atllovesmo5 to save $5🔮💫 Watch some crazy talented performers in drag, burlesque, and circus acts, shop with 40+ unique vendors,and experience interactive art installations. Don’t miss the dark forest edition on 4/20 at @westside_motor_lounge ! 

@paintnsitatl is a FREE event open to all. It’s Atlanta’s first free therapeutic art experience. They provide a community space that allows you to connect with like minded individuals through creative vulnerability and expression. Events are hosted at Old Fourth Ward Skatepark and various locations around the Atlanta Area. @paintnsitatl provides the space and supplies you need to create a masterpiece to keep or giveaway to their mobile community art gallery. Their next BIG event is June 10th so be sure to check it out. 

#atlart #atlevents #atlblog #thingstodoinatlanta

Date night but make it fun, part 5✨ follow @atllovesmo for more goodies 

@fernbankmuseum night at the museum is an obvious choice. Once a month they host fernbank after dark with live music, bartenders, and access to the exhibits (which are always offering something new). Tickets sell out & the next event is 3/8 so mark your calendars! Parking can be a little crazy so you may want to hire @pickyourleisure 😌

@thefriskywhiskeratl is at the top of my list for favorite places in Atlanta because where else can you sit back & relax with 25 of the sweetest cats 🐱 the space is unique as they’re also a sound gallery and art space. Find them in @underground_atlanta hosting paint & sip events and other listening parties. 

@stereoatl is the new hot spot in Atlanta (and a perfect museum pregame btw) with DJs spinning live vinyl while you sip on stirred or highball cocktails. It’s one of my favorite locations and the space is beautiful, plus they have charcuterie & indoor/ outdoor seating so you can chill for a while. Hop to over to @lloydspizzaparty for dinner. 

Have you been to any of these? Add this to your list when you want to do something different ✨ also note these are fun with a group of friends & even as a solo date, do your thinnnnggg 💫

#atlblog #thingstodoinatlanta #atleats #atlantafoodie

a few cool & funky experiences that would make for a fun night out with friends ✨

If you like exploring atlanta, follow @atllovesmo 💌

@mambozombi is a hidden bar above @gabeergarden on Edgewood giving spooky vibes with its coffin entrance and bizarre bathroom (you’ll see). My toxic trait is I always have to order the drink being lit on fire and they have plenty of cool cocktails on the menu. It’s a smaller space but it’s sure to be one of the most unique spots in atl. 

@thepigalle is one of my favorite new spots of 2023 located in @underground_atlanta. It’s a speakeasy x burlesque theatre x cabaret where you can sip absinthe cocktails and catch a show. Check out their calendar for upcoming events and more details. This quirky spot should absolutely be on your list of things to do. 

@theblindpigparlourbar in Buckhead has transformed in the spirit of Valentine’s day into The Blind Cupid. I always loove the ambiance as they go all out with decor! Time to get all cute with your galentines and grab a cocktail - reservations are open now. I’d have dinner at @storicofresco then stop in at the Blind Cupid for an after dinner drink. 

#atlfoodie #atlantafood #atleats #thingstodoinatlanta #atlblog

This is the best way to go on vacay without actually going on vacay ✨ I get questions about solo date night spots a lot- and these are perf for that!

follow @atllovesmo if you love to explore Atlanta 💌

I’m sure you’re ready to get out of the house post-holiday season so here are a few ideas for you. This is a series of vids you all loved this year. 

@verdureatlanta ➡️ is one of midtown’s prettiest farm-to-table restaurant right off the beltline. There are florals that adorn the ceiling and give in to the vibe of being in a hidden oasis. The menu is a fusion of Western & African ingredients. My favorites are the creamy lobster mac & cheese, the steak strip, & the chicken yassa. Don’t skip the cocktails bc they are over the top, like the creamy hibiscus margarita or the kiwi-passion margarita. Doesn’t have to be date night, this is also a great spot to get dressed up and have a GNO. 

@chicheriamx ➡️ transports you to the Baja-region! If you love hand-pressed blue corn tortillas (made daily), coastal flavors (that make you feel like you’re in Mexico), and delicious margaritas (I already know you do) - you’ll have to check out @chicheriamx in @theworksatl . Did not realize the caesar salad originated in Tijuana! We’ve all heard about girl dinner, and you’ll be sure to find me eating queso, a caesar salad, and the “you’ll never see daylight” margarita with bell pepper-infused tequila & strawberry syrup alll the time.

@yalda.atl ➡️ is a stunner on on the west side. The menu is an ode to @cookingwithashkan’s mothers cooking with delicious Persian recipes in an atmosphere that feels like you’re on vacation. The staff was incredibly helpful and the cocktails were as pretty as they were tasty. This is a great date night spot, GNO, or birthday spot! You can dine in the sunroom which feels European and when the weather is nice the windows from the patio open into the bar. The Sandy springs location is just as beautiful but this one brings a different vibe! 

#atleats #atldatenight #atlantafoodie #atldatenight

3 cozy spots to share with your date, friends, fam or save for yourself👇 

If you’re looking for recommendations in Atlanta, be sure to follow @atllovesmo💌

Word on the street is this garden restaurant is a favorite in Decatur. @wahoo_grill was homey and welcoming and giving local neighborhood bistro vibes. There’s a beautiful green space surrounding the dining room and I can’t wait to go back for a table in the garden. Went for the cheeseburger after hearing it recommended a few times and it did not disappoint (Allen Brothers, Pearson Farm apple chutney, brie spread, crispy pork belly). Plus you can’t go wrong with pimento cheese fritters and I’m still thinking about the salted caramel dessert. You do have to valet park if you aren’t parking across the street. Stop by next door @wahoowine to pick up a bottle on your way out. 

@lure.atl is a bungalow in midtown Atlanta that is also bringing the coziest of vibes. It’s a seafood restaurant and one you need to add to your happy hour list for $2 oysters, $7 hurricanes (rotating featured cocktail) and other deals on beer, wine, and food like $5 blackened fish tacos, and an $8 softshell crab bao. Happy hour is Mon-Sun from 4-6PM! Street parking is available. 

@rwbyatl has newly opened in midtown atl and it is a goodie. I’ve been obsessing over the floral bar and the cozy interior during dinner. The carrot dip is incredible and a must get appetizer. This would be a great solo dinner spot!! Go for one of their alcohol free cocktails, or try the amarcord spritz with cantaloupe or the waiting for cleo with ginger, honey, and lemon.

#atleats #atlblog #atlfoodie #atlanta #atlhappyhour

follow if these are your vibe 💌 this has become a series of some of my favorite spots to grab a drink - whether you’re going solo, to meet up with friends, or with a date. It’s the ambiance & the cocktails for me 🍸

@barpolitan in @politanrow.colonysquare is absolutely beautiful inside! I’m there for the cocktails and the pretty indoor/outdoor space. Parking is expensive so make sure you get it validated. 

@boldmonkbrewing is a go to date night spot on the westside, with a quiet library/bookstore upstairs & a really beautiful outdoor patio. Their food is good too! 

You already know my love for @hotelclermont runs deep & that includes the lobby bar which you need to explore because it is such a vibe. The bar serves some of my favorite cocktails like the espresso martini and the granada club. 

@yalda.atl is newly opened in west midtown and transports you to vacation with the greenery and decor. They have a great patio that opens up into the restaurant when the weather is nice & those cocktails were sooo good (like the longest night & the majnoon). I know it’s not the point of this post, but might as well grab a few bites to eat bc it’s delicious.

Save for your next outing ✨

Who did I miss? This is round 3 so head to my page or my cocktail hour guide for more!

